{"title":"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12A Problems\">2003 AMC 12A #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems\">2003 AMC 10A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many non-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent_(geometry)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent (geometry)\">congruent</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangles</a> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> have <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> side lengths? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad069be59a1dd259d51051fa77f3b9a9dd3b8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 1\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 2\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 3\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 4\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle inequality\">triangle inequality</a>, no side may have a length greater than the semiperimeter, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202ee6e52c56514e96fd7cb769f339f7d6a9eed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot7=3.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>Since all sides must be integers, the largest possible length of a side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, all such triangles must have all sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a62f5e8b629ef64f45bf2913a0e1f3051d14990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+2+2=6&lt;7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />, at least one side must have a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the remaining two sides have a combined length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd711fa530450bc7d279233a2d718766536fc0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-3=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. So, the remaining sides must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the number of triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8184dad25e7323b7229f452a12c5a00db2a0c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gII2tj5TZZY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gII2tj5TZZY</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A\">2003 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2003 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">Pr